n before merging","metadata index catalogues identify the survey used at each location"],"decision":"Persist the selected source survey and native resolution; a 1m composite cell must not be represented as a native 1m survey when its index reports a finer or coarser source."},{"id":"EA_COMPOSITE_INDEX_QUERYABLES","source":"Environment Agency OGC API Features","url":"https://environment.data.gov.uk/geoservices/datasets/9f0fa3fc-a860-4729-adc9-47fe53f658d0/ogc/features/v1/collections/LIDAR_Composite_1m_DTM_2022_extents/queryables?f=text%2Fhtml","role":"Composite tile and acquisition lineage","facts":["queryables include filename, tilename, polygon_id, resolution and year","queryables include od_dtm_fn, sd_flown and ed_flown","collection storage CRS is EPSG:27700"],"decision":"Parcel sampling manifest must bind the intersecting composite-index feature id and all listed lineage fields."},{"id":"EA_TIME_STAMPED_DTM_QUERYABLES","source":"Environment Agency OGC API Features","url":"https://environment.data.gov.uk/geoservices/datasets/9f0fa3fc-a860-4729-adc9-47fe53f658d0/ogc/features/v1/collections/LIDAR_DTM_Time_Stamped_Extents/queryables?f=text%2Fhtml","role":"Time-stamped source survey audit","facts":["queryables include lidar_name, dtm_name, tile and OS grid","survey start/end dates, year, season and resolution are exposed","returns, transform, geoid, archive, supplied and latest flags are exposed"],"decision":"When composite lineage resolves to a time-stamped survey, bind survey dates, resolution, return type, transform, geoid and latest flag; reject ambiguous matches."},{"id":"EA_NATIONAL_LIDAR_PROGRAMME_QUERYABLES","source":"Environment Agency OGC API Features","url":"https://environment.data.gov.uk/geoservices/datasets/9f0fa3fc-a860-4729-adc9-47fe53f658d0/ogc/features/v1/collections/National_LIDAR_Programme_Index_Catalogue/queryables?f=text%2Fhtml","role":"National LIDAR Programme source audit","facts":["queryables include DTM, DSM, first-return and point-cloud file